host_info(1)	    UNIX Programmer's Manual	     host_info(1)


NNAAMMEE
     hostinfo - display information about a Mach host

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     hostinfo

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The _h_o_s_t_i_n_f_o program displays information about a Mach host.
     In particular, it displays the maximum number of processors
     the kernel was configured for, the actual number of proces-
     sors physically available in the hardware configuration, and
     the amount of physical memory available in the host.  Then,
     for each logical slot, _h_o_s_t_i_n_f_o displays information about
     the processor configured in that slot.  The information
     includes the slot number, the cpu type and sub-type, whether
     or not the processor is executing, and finally, a summary of
     the processor utilization since boot time.  The processor
     utilization is split into user, system and idle time.

     The information provided by this program should be expanded
     in the future.  In addition, it should be possible to query
     other hosts in the network in future versions.

